        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "The **mass of a muon** is approximately:\n\n### 🟰 **1.883531627 × 10⁻²⁸ kilograms (kg)**  \n—or—  \n### 🟰 **105.6583755 MeV/c²** (in energy units)\n\nFor context:\n- A **muon** is a fundamental particle similar to the electron but about **207 times heavier**.\n- It has a negative electric charge (like the electron) and a spin of ½.\n- Muons are unstable and decay with a mean lifetime of about **2.2 microseconds**.\n\nWould you like a comparison between muons, electrons, and tau particles?"
